<p>A banner is read in half a second, and every device shows a different crop of it: a desk sees a band 2560 wide and 423 tall through the middle, a TV sees all of it, a phone sees 1546 × 423 in the centre. So this one is built the way the site is built. The <strong>page</strong> is the grid, edge to edge, and lying across the band is a <strong>cover</strong>: white, a hairline, faint scanlines, a key light where the portrait is. Inside the phone’s 1546: a greeting in Devanagari, the name with the brand’s dot after it, two facts in the mono face, one line in the hand, the website and the mail. A dashed trail from India to Budapest with a plane on it. The illustration — the portrait with its golden circle — rising out of the cover on the right, and six floating tiles round it, each with a hand-written word: build, ai, vlogs, travel, party. For the desk and the TV only: the follow row on the left, the schedule on the right.</p>
