<h2>Anatomy</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>The page</td><td><code>im-studio-banner im-studio-cream</code> + <code>im-studio-bg im-bg-grid</code></td><td>Warm paper and the grid at 64px. The whole 2560 × 1440; the TV sees it all.</td></tr>
<tr><td>The cover</td><td><code>im-studio-banner-cover</code></td><td>The band from 508px down, 423 tall. White, a hairline, scanlines and a key light as pseudo-elements, a soft shadow on the page. Everything else is positioned inside it, in its own em.</td></tr>
<tr><td>The art</td><td><code>im-studio-banner-art</code></td><td>The illustration, placed so its golden circle meets the cover’s top edge and the cover cuts the rest. <code>-photo</code> takes a photograph instead, faded at both sides.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Intro</td><td><code>im-studio-banner-intro</code></td><td><code>im-studio-greeting</code> (Devanagari, the accent), the title with the wordmark’s dot, <code>im-studio-facts</code> with icons, the line in the hand (<code>im-studio-note</code>), the links in the accent.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Trail</td><td><code>im-studio-banner-trail</code> + <code>im-studio-badge</code> + <code>im-studio-pill</code></td><td>A dashed SVG path in the accent, a plane in a badge, the two places as pills.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tiles</td><td><code>im-studio-tilelabel</code> &gt; <code>im-studio-tile</code> + <code>im-studio-note</code></td><td>A white square with an icon, tilted, and a hand-written word under it. Six of them, each placed with <code>im-studio-at</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Follow</td><td><code>im-studio-banner-follow</code> + <code>im-studio-socials</code></td><td>Outside the phone’s band: a label and four ringed brand marks.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Schedule</td><td><code>im-studio-banner-schedule</code> + <code>im-studio-slot</code></td><td>Outside the band on the right: the live stream with the dot, the new video with the play mark, each with its day and time.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>Change the words, keep the art</h2>
<p>Everything on the cover is live text. The greeting, the name, the facts, the line, the tile words and the schedule are the strings in <code>site/pages/frames/channel-art.hbs</code>; the picture is <code>demo.art</code> (<code>/assets/brand/cover.png</code>). Export it with <code>npm run frames channel-art</code>, or rebuild it as layers in Pixelmator with <a href="/content-creation/youtube/pixelmator/">the template script</a> and move the tiles by hand.</p>
